{{also|in-kind}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{calque|en|la|in specie}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|title=kind|code=103444|part of speech=n}} (section 15. “in kind”)</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-in kind.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Prepositional phrase===
{{head|en|prepositional phrase}}

# {{lb|en|usually after the noun}} In the form of [[goods]] and [[services]] rather than [[money]].
#* {{quote-book|en|page=13|chapter=[[:s:Treaty of friendship and commerce between Great Britain and Siam/Treaty|Treaty signed April 18, 1855; ratified April 5, 1856]]|title=Treaty of friendship and commerce between Great Britain and Siam|year=1856|publisher=J. H. Chandler|location=Bangkok|text=On all articles of import the duties shall be three per cent, payable at the option of the importer, either '''in kind''' or money, calculated upon the market value of the goods.}}
#: {{ux|en|In the era before the widespread monetization of transactions with currency, barter was the usual form of selling and buying for farmers, and payment of taxes was often '''in kind'''; that is, farmers' payment method was most often their produce itself.}}
#: {{ux|en|How much did he give? – Hard to say. It was all '''in kind'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The pay is OK, but the real attraction is all the benefits '''in kind'''.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|benefit in kind}}
* {{l|en|payment in kind}}
* {{l|en|grant in kind}}
* {{l|en|tax in kind}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|of [[pay]]ing or [[give|giving]]}} With [[good]]s or [[service]]s (as opposed to [[cash]]).
#: {{syn|en|in trade}}
#: {{ant|en|in cash}}
#: {{ux|en|I made some donations to the charity, not in money, but '''in kind''', such as non-perishable food.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} In a [[reciprocal]] manner; in a similar way; in the same kind.
#: {{syn|en|equivalently|reciprocally|similarly}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Alan Smith|title=Leicester City back on top as Riyad Mahrez hat-trick downs Swansea City|work={{w|The Guardian}} (London)|date=5 December 2015|url=http://www.theguardian.com/football/2015/dec/05/swansea-city-leicester-city-premier-league-match-report
|passage=Vardy drilled over after getting behind Bartley and also hit the side-netting, resulting in the loudest cheer of the day from the Swansea fans after he kicked an advertising board in frustration. He responded '''in kind''' by showing them three fingers with one hand and making a zero with the other.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Drachinifel|title=Guadalcanal Campaign - The Big Night Battle: Night 1 (IJN 3(?) : 2 USN)|date=10 March 2021|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Em_PuLURII4|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221017005233/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Em_PuLURII4|archivedate=17 October 2022|accessdate=6 November 2022|time=17:51|text=Armor-piercing shells ''were'' heading up the shell hoists, but this procedure took a few minutes, allowing the battered American flagship to reply '''in kind''', the gunners ''somewhat motivated'' to set new records for the rate of fire as the cruiser raked the larger ship from stem to stern in response.}}

====Usage notes====
Frequently in the phrase ''payment '''in kind'''.''

